  "result": "**What it does:** Order utility module — computes cart totals (`calcTotal`), applies discount codes (`applyDiscount`), averages item price (`averageItemPrice`), and formats an order as a printable string (`formatOrder`).\n\n**Bug found:**\n- `calcTotal` (line 5): loop condition is `i <= items.length` instead of `i < items.length`. This runs one iteration past the array end, so `items[items.length]` is `undefined` and `.price`/`.qty` on it throws a `TypeError`. This breaks every caller (`averageItemPrice`, `formatOrder` too, since they call `calcTotal`).\n\nMinor: `averageItemPrice` divides by `items.length` with no guard, so an empty array yields `NaN` (would surface once the above bug is fixed).",
